{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Sell it as of today.</b> Rashi explained etc. — as he said: a priest who has killed a person may not lift his hands, and all the more so may not perform the divine service; and at that time the divine service belonged to the firstborn. Another interpretation: Jacob said — a person is obligated in honor to his older brother, and this wicked man is not worthy of honor. 'As of today' — now, when the divine service is not yet in effect; but in the future, when the divine service belongs to the firstborn, a person may not purchase the firstborn status. Another interpretation: <b>sell it as of today</b> — immediately, just as 'this day' is immediate. That is: sell me right now, for money that I will give you, your firstborn portion that is due to you from our father's property. Another interpretation: <b>as of today</b> — according to what it is worth today, and that is a small amount, for how many births may yet come into the matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The opening citation reads 'פרש״י וכו׳' (Rashi explained etc.), which appears to be Chizkuni's way of referencing Rashi's comment without reproducing it in full. The phrase 'כמה נולדות יש לבא בדבר' in the last interpretation is rendered literally; it likely refers to the fact that future births (additional siblings) would dilute the firstborn's monetary share, making it worth little today."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:02.487913406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}